  "answer": "A past ticket (PowerToys#45452) reports the same symptom. A Ctrl+key shortcut (Ctrl+W there) stopped working in every app while Command Palette was enabled, and worked again once it was disabled. The cause was a leftover per-command hotkey in Command Palette's settings. It had been assigned to a top-level command from an extension that was later uninstalled, and Command Palette kept intercepting it. Your ticket doesn't confirm this is the cause for you, but it's worth checking. Open %localappdata%\\Packages\\Microsoft.CommandPalette_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\LocalState\\settings.json and look in the \"CommandHotkeys\" array for an entry with \"ctrl\": true and \"code\": 66 (the B key). If one is there and you don't want it, delete it. Ticket 45452 says the key works again right away after that. You can also remove the hotkey from the command's settings inside Command Palette. If there is no such entry, upload a PowerToys Report Bug zip and your settings.json to the ticket so it can be investigated further."
 },
